.TH KISA-CCE-POLICY-COMPILE 8 "2026-09-04" "KISA CCE Linux Scanner" "System Administration Commands"
.SH NAME
kisa-cce-policy-compile \- compile policy YAML into scanner policy TSV
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kisa-cce-policy-compile
.BI \-\-input " FILE"
.BI \-\-output-dir " PATH"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kisa-cce-policy-compile
converts a restricted policy YAML file into the strict TSV directory read by
.BR kisa-cce-scan (8).
The scanner itself does not parse YAML.
.PP
The compiler implements a YAML subset without a YAML library. It accepts
only schema version 1, block lists with fixed mappings, full-line comments,
plain scalars, and quoted scalars with a restricted escape set.
Anchors, aliases, tags, merge keys, flow collections, block scalars, multiple
documents, tabs, carriage returns, and inline comments in plain scalars are
rejected.  ASCII and Unicode C1 control characters and malformed UTF-8 are
also rejected.
.PP
Before publishing output, the compiler reloads the generated directory with
the scanner's canonical policy validator. This rejects invalid criterion
codes, decisions, review IDs, dates, providers, source identities, duplicate
entries, and invalid expiration-field syntax.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-input " FILE"
Read the policy YAML from
.IR FILE .
The path may be relative to the current directory. The file must be readable,
regular, owned by root or the effective user, and not writable by group or
other users. Symbolic links and untrusted parent paths are rejected.
.TP
.BI \-\-output-dir " PATH"
Create a new compiled policy directory at
.IR PATH .
The target must not exist, and its parent must be a trusted physical
directory. The compiler never overwrites an existing path.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print command help and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the scanner version and policy YAML schema version, then exit.
.SH YAML SCHEMA
The document must begin with the schema declaration and an attestation list:
.PP
.EX
schema_version: 1
attestations:
  - code: U-07
    decision: GOOD
    review_id: sha256:0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef
    ticket: IAM-2026-0142
    approver: identity-governance
    expires: 2026-12-31
.EE
.PP
.B attestations
is required and may be the explicit empty list
.BR [] .
Attestation review IDs must come from a current policy-class audit result.
Current audits use review-basis schema 2, which includes the resolution class
and the complete redacted result basis. Review schema 1 IDs do not match
current results.
The optional
.B time_sources
list uses provider, host, address, ticket, approver, and expires fields.
Supported provider values are
.BR chrony ,
.BR ntpd-rs ,
.BR ntpsec ,
and
.BR systemd-timesyncd .
The ntpd-rs value limits the source approval to a selected ntpd-rs
installation. Chrony remains the Ubuntu 26.04 default.
Omitting the time_sources list leaves the typed fact set absent. Writing
.B "time_sources: []"
explicitly approves an empty source set. Use it only when that is the
intended policy decision.
.PP
Mapping fields may appear in any order. Every required field must occur
exactly once. Indent list markers with two spaces and continuation fields with
four. Full-line comments and blank lines are accepted. Use single or double
quotes for values that would be ambiguous as plain scalars in this grammar.
Within double quotes, only an escaped double quote or backslash is accepted.
Within single quotes, one quote is represented by two consecutive quotes.
.SH OUTPUT
On success, the compiler creates an owner-only directory containing
.I 50-compiled.tsv
and, when
.B time_sources
was supplied,
.IR facts/time-sources.tsv .
Directories use mode 0700 and files use mode 0600.
.PP
Every terminal line uses the dmesg-style scanner prefix. On success, the
compiler prints:
.PP
.EX
[    12.345678] kisa-cce-policy-compile: policy_directory=/absolute/path
[    12.345678] kisa-cce-policy-compile: policy_digest=sha256:HEX_DIGEST
.EE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The generated directory passed structural checks and the scanner's canonical
policy validation.
.TP
.B 2
Invocation, path validation, YAML parsing, policy validation, or publication
failed.  No completed output directory is reported.
.SH SECURITY
The wrapper clears the caller environment before loading Bash code. The
compiler parses YAML as data; it never sources or evaluates it. File
descriptors pin the input and output directories. Publication uses a
no-replace rename in the target parent.
.PP
Compilation validates the policy format; it does not authorize the decisions.
Administrators remain responsible for the review IDs, tickets, approvers, and
expiration dates.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/kisa-cce-scanner/policy.d/
Default installed policy directory consumed by complete and automation scans.
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/kisa-cce-linux-scanner/examples/policy.yml
A package may install the source example here. The upstream
.B make install
target does not install repository documentation or examples.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR kisa-cce-scan (8)
